# Hebrew RTL responses

When the user writes in Hebrew, answer in Hebrew. Never leave Hebrew prose in left-to-right layout.

- Wrap the entire Hebrew reply in `<div dir="rtl" align="right">...</div>`.
- Put headings, paragraphs, lists, and tables inside that wrapper so they render right to left.
- Keep code, commands, paths, identifiers, and technical values in their original left-to-right form.
- Do not mix unwrapped Hebrew sentences outside the RTL wrapper.
